<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Idi Amin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1925–2003</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Idi Amin was a Ugandan army officer who seized power from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> in 1971. He expelled Uganda's Asian community in 1972, and his regime killed tens of thousands of people. His invasion of the Kagera region of Tanzania in 1978 led to a Tanzanian counter-invasion that overthrew him in 1979, and he died in exile in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/idi-amin.jpg" alt="Idi Amin" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gotfryd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Idi_Amin_at_UN_(United_Nations,_New_York)_gtfy.00132_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
